# __AGENT_NAME__ Brain — HOME

The index of the curated markdown memory layer. Keep this page current: it is
the first thing retrieval finds and the map future-you navigates by.

## Structure

```
vault/brain/
├── architecture/    system designs, how things fit together
├── companies/       organisations, products, vendors
├── concepts/        mental models, frameworks
├── continuity/      machine-maintained status pages (capture health, etc.)
├── conversations/   distilled outcomes of important exchanges
├── daily/           date-keyed notes, consolidated nightly
├── guides/          runbooks, how-tos
├── meetings/        meeting outcomes and decisions
├── people/          contacts, collaborators
├── projects/        multi-session work arcs
├── sources/         provenance for imported material
└── tech/            technical references
```

## Filing rules

- File by **PRIMARY SUBJECT**, not format or source. A meeting about Project X
  updates `projects/project-x.md`, not a new meetings page.
- **Cross-link compulsively** with `[[wiki-links]]` — links are what make the
  brain a graph instead of a pile.
- Update pages **in place**; never create dated dump pages outside `daily/`.
- Frontmatter on every page: `title`, `type`, `date`, `tags`.
- No secrets, no PII beyond what the work needs, no raw transcripts.

## Memory stack

| Layer | Where | Job |
|-------|-------|-----|
| Bootstrap | `memories/MEMORY.md` + `USER.md` | always-loaded compact facts |
| Semantic brain | this directory via GBrain | searchable knowledge base |
| Daily notes | `daily/` | working memory, consolidated nightly |
